From c3e3f50ee4b2b54756deb11892094562886d0a1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dennis Klappe <dennisklappe@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 14:19:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Lift the licence gate on guest accounts in the web app

The server side (patch 0011) makes guest accounts follow
GuestAccountsSettings.Enable alone, but the web app still hid or upsold every
entry point, so the feature was unreachable. Removes the licence checks at:

  admin_console/admin_definition.tsx
      Guest Access renders the real settings page; the feature-discovery
      upsell that replaced it is dropped.
  permission_schemes_settings/permission_system_scheme_settings
  permission_schemes_settings/permission_team_scheme_settings
      the Guests permission panel follows EnableGuestAccounts alone.
  channel_invite_modal/index.ts
      canInviteGuests keys off BuildEnterpriseReady, matching invitation_modal.
  invitation_modal/invite_as.tsx
      only a cloud starter plan still restricts the Guest option; an
      unlicensed self-hosted server no longer gets the upsell badge.
  admin_console/system_users/system_users_list_actions
      "Demote to guest" follows GuestAccountsSettings.Enable.

The two invite_as tests that asserted the self-hosted starter upsell now
assert the opposite.

See https://mattermore.dev/guest-accounts
